<title>UK: BAA dips after in-line profit figures.</title>
<headline>BAA dips after in-line profit figures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BAA Plc were down 3p to 529p by 0835 GMT after the UK airports group reported a 6.2 percent rise in nine month pre-tax profit to 397 million stg.</p>
<p>The market forecast ranged from 392 million stg to 400 million stg.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a steady result but nothing terribly exciting,&quot; one senior dealer said. &quot;The overall market is a bit weak this morning and the shares are just reflecting that weakness.&quot;</p>
<p>The FTSE 100 index was down 4.1 points at 4,271.7.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
